Programs whose recorded run is gcon-vm's, not gcon's Go VM's (recorded
with tests/expected.sh -accept), and why.

ipl-progs/ifncsgen       function() generates the graphics functions,
                         as a graphics iconx's does (the Go VM has none)
ipl-progs/irunerr        the error texts include 140-147 (graphics)
tests-general/features   &features includes "dynamic loading",
                         "external values" and "graphics", each with its
                         predefined symbol (gcon now predefines the
                         runtime's: _DYNAMIC_LOADING, _EXTERNAL_VALUES,
                         _GRAPHICS)
tests-general/prepro     the same symbols: its output is now iconx's
                         prepro.std exactly (the Go VM, lacking the
                         features, reports "unexpected predefined symbol")
tests-general/features   gcon predefines _X_WINDOW_SYSTEM (its events use X
                         keysyms, which the IPL's keysyms.icn names under
                         it), so &features includes "X Windows" (icon-sdl
                         defines _SDL_GRAPHICS instead)
ipl-progs/ifncsgen       function() now generates DrawCurve, DrawImage,
                         PaletteChars, PaletteColor, PaletteKey, ReadImage
                         and WriteImage, and the graphics functions have
                         iconx's arities (args()): identical to icon-sdl's
                         iconx but for gcon's own bytes, len, runes, uchar
                         and utf8valid
